{#- docs/sprint_<n>_summary.md - the Sprint Record: one document per sprint,
    carrying every attempt made at it.

    The block down to "Attempt History" is parsed by the sprint panel in the UI
    (langchain-ui/src/components/SprintSummaryPanel.tsx): its bold field labels,
    the bullets under "Planned for This Sprint" and "Features Implemented", and
    the `- [STATUS] description (Owner: role)` lines under "Defect Summary" - the
    check that raised a defect goes before "(Owner:", never after it. The
    sections after it must never produce a line of that last shape - the panel
    reads defect lines from "Defect Summary" to the end of the file.

    Context is prepared by `app.agents.sprint_summary.render_sprint_summary`. -#}
# Sprint {{ number }}{{ of_plan }} Summary

**Goal:** {{ goal or "Unknown goal" }}
**Status:** {{ status }}{{ (", without " ~ (deferred | join(", ")) ~ ": deferred because they could not be made to pass, so this sprint did not deliver them") if deferred else "" }}
**Attempts:** {{ attempts_line }}
{% if reason %}
**Failure Reason:** {{ reason }}
{% endif %}
**Test Cases:** {{ cases.tests if cases else "not reported" }}
- **Passed:** {{ cases.passed if cases else 0 }}
- **Failed:** {{ cases.failed if cases else 0 }}

## Planned for This Sprint
{{ planned | bullets("- Nothing recorded from the sprint plan.") }}

## Features Implemented
{% if not completed %}
These are the tasks this sprint delegated, not a record of what passed: the sprint did not pass its review, so read them as what was attempted.
{% endif %}
{{ features | bullets("- No delegated work recorded.") }}

## Test Cycles
- **Rounds Completed:** {{ rounds }}
- **Total Bugs Found:** {{ tally.found }}
- **Bugs Fixed:** {{ tally.fixed }}
- **Bugs Open:** {{ tally.open }}
{% if defects %}

### Defect Summary
{% for d in defects %}
- [{{ d.status | upper }}] {{ d.description }}{{ (" - raised by " ~ d.source) if d.source else "" }} (Owner: {{ d.owner }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if history %}

## Attempt History
Every attempt at *this* sprint, oldest first. A re-run is a second attempt at one sprint, not an extra sprint.
{% for line in history %}
- {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Work Orders
{% for w in work_orders %}

### {{ loop.index }}. {{ w.title }} — {{ w.role }}
- **Outcome:** {{ w.outcome }}
- **Files planned:** {{ w.files_planned | join(", ") | text("not stated") }}
- **Files changed:** {{ w.files_changed | join(", ") | text("none reported") }}
- **Verification:** {{ w.verification | join("; ") | text("none recorded") }}
- **Blockers raised:** {{ w.blockers | join("; ") | text("none") }}
{% else %}
None recorded.
{% endfor %}

## Defect Log
{% for d in defect_log %}

### {{ d.id }} · {{ d.severity }} · {{ d.state }}
- **Summary:** {{ d.description | text }}
- **Owner:** {{ d.owner | text }}
- **Reproduction:** {{ d.reproduction | text }}
- **Expected:** {{ d.expected | text }}
- **Actual:** {{ d.actual | text }}
- **Files:** {{ d.files | join(", ") | text("not identified") }}
- **How it was fixed:** {{ d.resolution | text("not recorded") }}
- **Fix verified by:** {{ d.verified_by | text("nothing recorded") }}
- **Regression test:** {{ d.regression_test | text("none named") }}
{% else %}
No defects were found.
{% endfor %}

